<section class="landing-section features" style="flex-shrink: 0; box-sizing: border-box; padding: 112px 120px; background: var(--surface); border-top: 1px solid var(--line); border-bottom: 1px solid var(--line); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 44px">
  <div style="display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 16px; max-width: 900px">
    <div style="font-family: 'Geist Mono', ui-monospace, monospace; font-size: 13px; color: var(--accent)">06 · in the box</div>
    <h2 style="margin: 0; font-family: 'Instrument Serif', Georgia, serif; font-weight: 400; font-size: 64px; line-height: 1; letter-spacing: -0.015em">Built by people who review code every day, and resented every minute of it.</h2>
  </div>
  <div data-grid="three" style="display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 20px">
    <div style="padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--surface-soft); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M3 12h18"></path><circle cx="9" cy="12" r="3" fill="var(--surface)"></circle><path d="M3 6h6M3 18h12"></path></svg>
      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3">Got time for 37 files, or 13?</h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">Drag the review-depth slider from Essential to Complete. The files most likely to break production open first.</p>
      <div style="margin-top: auto; display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(4, minmax(0, 1fr)); gap: 4px; font-size: 11px; text-align: center; color: var(--muted)"><span style="padding: 6px 0; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--on-solid)">Essential</span><span style="padding: 6px 0; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--blue-tint)">Focused</span><span style="padding: 6px 0; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--muted-surface)">Careful</span><span style="padding: 6px 0; border-radius: 6px; background: var(--muted-surface)">Complete</span></div>
    </div>
    <div style="padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--surface-soft); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="3" y="4" width="18" height="16" rx="2"></rect><path d="M7 9h6M7 13h8M7 17h4M17 9v8"></path></svg>
      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3">Know which model wrote the line.</h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">With GitClear's telemetry hooks installed, an authorship gutter names the model behind each attributed line, beside a per-file AI percentage.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--surface-soft); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 12a8 8 0 1 0 2.3-5.7"></path><path d="M4 4v4h4"></path><path d="M12 8v4l3 2"></path></svg>
      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3">Come back to a long PR, see only what's new.</h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">Files you've read show only their new commits; files you haven't show everything. One click restores the full diff against main.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--surface-soft); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M21 15a2 2 0 0 1-2 2H8l-5 4V5a2 2 0 0 1 2-2h14a2 2 0 0 1 2 2z"></path></svg>
      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3">The author already explained it.</h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">Hover any line for the commit message behind its last meaningful change, plus its Diff Delta. No separate blame pane.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--surface-soft); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="2.5"></circle><circle cx="18" cy="18" r="2.5"></circle><path d="M6 8.5v3a4 4 0 0 0 4 4h5.5"></path></svg>
      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3">Blame that keeps going. <span style="font-size: 12px; font-weight: 600; padding: 2px 7px; border-radius: 5px; background: var(--ink); color: var(--on-solid); vertical-align: middle">Pro</span></h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">Follow a line back through function moves, file renames and find-replaces, including how much of it began with an AI assistant.</p>
    </div>
    <div style="padding: 28px; border: 1px solid var(--line); border-radius: 16px; background: var(--surface-soft); display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 14px">
      <svg width="28" height="28" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="var(--accent)" stroke-width="1.8" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="10" width="16" height="11" rx="2"></rect><path d="M8 10V7a4 4 0 0 1 8 0v3"></path></svg>
      <h3 style="margin: 0; font-size: 20px; font-weight: 600; line-height: 1.3">Offline-first, on your laptop.</h3>
      <p style="margin: 0; font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.6; color: var(--body)">Source never leaves your machine. The app ships its own git, Ruby and PostgreSQL, and keeps itself up to date.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
